      "id": 1,
      "text": "Orrtanna began as a railway stop called Orr Station in 1885, anchoring the community along the Baltimore and Harrisburg Railway.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orrtanna%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name evolved from Wortzville, after businessman George Wortz, to Orr Station, and finally to Orrtanna.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orrtanna%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1913 John S. founded the Orrtanna Canning Company, a local industry that later became a focal point for labor activism.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orrtanna%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "October 1919 saw about thirty women apple peelers walk out of the canning plant, joining a broader movement for better wages in Pennsylvania’s food factories.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orrtanna%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The 1975 opening of the Adams County Winery made it Pennsylvania’s fifth oldest operating winery, while Hickory Bridge Farm began as a bed and breakfast in 1977.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orrtanna%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
